config SID_END_DEVICE_NOTIFY_DATA_PERIOD_MS
    int "Notify period of sensor monitoring demo app"
    default 300000
    help
      How often the app TX thread wakes up to sample sensors and send a telemetry
      uplink. Sidewalk gateways enforce per-device duty-cycle and message-rate
      limits, and this uplink competes for airtime with the Memfault chunk drain
      (its own timer, see CONFIG_SID_END_DEVICE_MEMFAULT_DRAIN_INTERVAL_S). Each
      notify period sends more than one uplink -- the demo binary notify and the
      JSON telemetry payload -- and the drain adds two more chunks, so a short
      period floods the message log. 5 minutes is about 12 telemetry uplinks an
      hour, which still looks live on a dashboard without burying everything
      else. Tune it per deployment: shorter for a bench demo next to a gateway,
      longer for a battery-powered field unit.

config SID_END_DEVICE_NOTIFY_CAPABILITY_RETRY_INITIAL_S
    int "Initial capability resend interval"
    range 1 3600
    default 30
    help
      How soon after time sync succeeds the device first resends the capability
      discovery message if the cloud has not acknowledged it yet. Deliberately
      decoupled from CONFIG_SID_END_DEVICE_NOTIFY_DATA_PERIOD_MS: the capability
      message is low-value traffic (its payload is empty on boards with no
      sensors) and should not be forced onto the same cadence as telemetry.

config SID_END_DEVICE_NOTIFY_CAPABILITY_RETRY_MAX_S
    int "Maximum capability resend interval"
    range 1 3600
    default 300
    help
      Upper bound for the capability resend backoff. Each unacknowledged resend
      doubles the wait, capped here, so a device that never receives a capability
      ack (no downlink support, or the network has none to send) settles at one
      resend every 5 minutes instead of hammering the network on every notify
      period forever.

